{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Provision the statusd service owner, status-reader account, outsider account, and status-readers role with the intended membership boundary.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The accounts and group exist; status-reader is a member of status-readers, while outsider is not. These identities and memberships persisted after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9d1d87aabcc7412e","cmd-2a6d5c622f474108"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Repair and operate server.py on /srv/legacy2/unix-socket-access-boundary/run/status.sock, accessible only to statusd and status-readers members.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The service runs as statusd with group status-readers. The socket is statusd:status-readers mode 0660; both the owner and authorized reader connected successfully, while outsider received PermissionError. The service and access boundary recovered after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6e44ac0f571f49bb","cmd-17b73339c7e442d9","cmd-8cfbacc012054812","cmd-2a6d5c622f474108"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Return the supplied status document for exactly STATUS followed by a newline, and an error for other requests.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Authorized STATUS requests returned branch=west/state=ready, while NOPE, INVALID, and OTHER requests returned ERROR. The captured server implementation also branches on the exact byte sequence STATUS\\n.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f1b63efc44ef410e","cmd-17b73339c7e442d9","cmd-8cfbacc012054812","cmd-2a6d5c622f474108"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Preserve the supplied status document.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The document retained SHA-256 5b47f32d92c3ae9661d765212aa884f1610132293932355cfac4dc28b94f305b from the authored baseline through repair and the post-restart state, and its returned content remained unchanged.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-f1b63efc44ef410e","cmd-8cfbacc012054812","cmd-2a6d5c622f474108"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use legacy-platform-compatible software.","status":"satisfied","summary":"RHEL 9.8 and kernel 5.14.0-687.20.1.el9_8.x86_64 were unchanged. The implementation uses the platform's existing /usr/bin/python3 runtime, with no package installation recorded.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6f76ff0a79f442b5","cmd-9d1d87aabcc7412e","cmd-2a6d5c622f474108","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Account/group creation in cmd-9d1d87aabcc7412e and the server, permissions, and service changes in cmd-f1b63efc44ef410e directly implemented the task. Although cmd-f1b63efc44ef410e exited nonzero because its immediate socket stat raced service startup, its intended changes succeeded and subsequent evidence showed a healthy socket and service. The restart scheduled by cmd-f1a5f47cf7bf4889 was required by the provider evidence protocol. No failed services, package damage, unrelated network exposure, or abandoned temporary artifacts were observed afterward.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9d1d87aabcc7412e","cmd-f1b63efc44ef410e","cmd-6e44ac0f571f49bb","cmd-f1a5f47cf7bf4889","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete: node1 was healthy before restart, the restart was acknowledged, boot identity changed from 3aee314b-4dfc-4c3a-90f6-2b07c621eaa0 to 4b3575fe-c558-43f4-83b8-c0a096e034cd, and system, service, identities, document, socket permissions, and protocol behavior recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the change.","limitations":["Invalid-request behavior was directly sampled with several representative requests rather than exhaustively tested across every possible byte sequence; the captured implementation supports the general result.","Lifecycle listening-socket snapshots inventory network sockets and therefore do not independently show the Unix-domain socket; direct executor observations provide that evidence."]}
